Z||000005||87ECO5||07-13-2000||09:13 PM||||WOW!!!!!  $350 for that!?  That's a lot of money for that thing!  Anybody want to take a guess on what it returns horsepower-wise?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/intake_tube.gif"> <P>BTW, this item is under their "SPECIALS" section on the online catalog.  Also, it doesn't say but it looks like it'll only fit the V6.||||reg||9
Z||000006||terryk||07-14-2000||12:33 AM||||Hey, K&N says it's better, so it must be!||||reg||1
Z||000007||ThatRickGuy||07-14-2000||07:59 AM||||It is K&N so it is better. $300 better? no, but better. K&N filters flow better then stock filters and even better then no filter. I've seen 1/4 mile slips showing all 3 runs same day, with just changing the filter, not a huge difference, but when you figure you buy a $50 filter, and it can be cleaned/reused (never having to buy another one) and it will get you a bit of a power improvment on top, well, K&N makes good products. Not sure about that chrome pipe tho...||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||07-14-2000||03:07 PM||||Ive got a pretty modified 3.1 w/turbo. I have a Ferrari kit body and use the body side scoop to 'ram' fresh air to OEM air filter canister. Replaced original filter with K&N. works fine. but u do have to occasionly check inside canister for rust that loosens paint on the inside and can send it thru your throttlebody and intake.||||reg||1
Z||000009||terryk||07-14-2000||05:38 PM||||I guess I'm trying to figure out where the K&N air filter is used on the top fueler in the commerical........||||reg||12
Z||000010||chris west||07-14-2000||08:25 PM||||Hey guys this is Will here at West Coast Fiero. We are puting a new cold air intake system on to the market some of u that we at the west fest last week may have seen it. It uses a freeflow filter and mounts next to the side scoop and the air temp sensor fits as it does in the factory setup. You will b able to see some pictures of how it looks on our site in a week or two. Unlike the fiero shops $350 intake that doesnt go to the cold air ours is only $250 and gets nice cold air for ur motor.||||reg||3
Z||000011||86se/lambo||07-16-2000||01:07 AM||||i have a better idea. measure the inside diameter of the black intake pipe at the air box. go to your local k&n dealer and ask then for a cone filter to fit that opening. if they dont have one they will order it. they have them.. thats what i did. i sliced a small x into the end of the filter and inserted the air temp sensor. talk obout sucking air!! but you gotta keep the old air box for smog purposes. i think the cost was about $50.||||reg||1
